2026-09-27T09:10:34.2552539Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2552749Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553046Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553323Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553420Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553629Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553747Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2553909Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2554292Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2554526Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2554641Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2554942Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2555135Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2555268Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2555672Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2556033Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2556731Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2557303Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2557416Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2557870Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2558630Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2558933Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2629594Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2630118Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2630223Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2630443Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2630555Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2632084Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2633444Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2633711Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2634199Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2635159Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2635750Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2636334Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2636813Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2637221Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2637335Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2637585Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2637734Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2638935Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2640095Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2640758Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2641689Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:34.2641908Z 
